      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 19th century, Quakers in Friendsville helped spark abolitionist movements in Blount County before the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friendsville%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A cave near the Friends Meetinghouse once stocked supplies for more than 2,000 fugitives traveling north on the Underground Railroad.",
